VERDICT: REJECTED
The diff introduces substantial UI/API scaffolding for website pages and bookings, but it does not satisfy multiple core functional requirements and contains blocking gating/state issues.

Critical findings:
1) Add-on activation cannot reliably work end-to-end. `websiteAddonActive` is used throughout routes/UI, but the `users` schema shown in this diff does not include `websiteAddonActive`/`websiteAddonSubscriptionId` fields. That makes add-on state persistence and retrieval non-functional (or runtime-error-prone) in this code path.
2) Cancellation/entitlement enforcement is incomplete. Public website endpoint (`GET /api/site/:slug`) only checks `isPublished`; it does not verify active add-on status. This violates the requirement that cancelling the add-on disables the public site while preserving data.
3) Required DB migration is missing. New tables were added to `shared/schema.ts`, but no migration file was added (migrations directory still only has `1689_create_agent_messages.sql`). This is a deployment blocker.
4) Owner-booking APIs are missing required add-on gating. `GET/PATCH /api/my-website/bookings` allow authenticated access without checking paid plan + add-on active, contrary to requirements.
5) Feature behavior diverges from spec in important areas: templates render full inline menu instead of optionVERDICT: REJECTED
